<p>Stories and the site design are owned by {{ site.operator }} unless a page says otherwise. {{ site.name }} is a trade name of {{ site.operator }}, {{ site.entityDescription }}. Quotes from sources remain the property of their publishers. Public records and government pages keep their own status.</p>
<p>You may share a link. You may quote a short passage with credit and a link to the article. You may not copy articles for commercial republication or present our wording as your own. The <a href="{{ '/terms/' | url }}">terms of use</a> say the same thing.</p>
<h2>Copyright complaints</h2>
<p>If you believe material on this site infringes a copyright you own, send a notice through the <a href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}">contact form</a>. We do not publish a street address, and this page does not appoint a registered agent. Include:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Your name and an email address where you can be reached.</li>
  <li>A description of the copyrighted work.</li>
  <li>The URL of the material you believe infringes it.</li>
  <li>A statement that you have a good-faith belief the use is not authorized by the copyright owner, its agent, or the law.</li>
  <li>A statement that the information in the notice is accurate, and under penalty of perjury that you are the owner or are authorized to act for the owner.</li>
  <li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
</ul>
<p>If the notice is complete and the claim is sound, we will remove or correct the material. If we need more detail, we will reply to the email address you gave. A notice that asks us to take down sourced reporting you simply disagree with is not a copyright complaint. Factual corrections go through the <a href="{{ '/corrections/' | url }}">corrections</a> page.</p>
